{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011WPv6LcMDey174Q9gyewiR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — exec-sim-repair-verifier\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Extended fallback: ICSE 2027 (Jun 23 abstract, Jun 30 paper)\n7\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (9 days remaining)\n8\t\n9\t## D116 Framing Pivot (2026-05-16)\n10\t\n11\t**前 framing**: \"CLS scales where generation fails\" (CLS advocacy)\n12\t**新 framing**: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n13\t\n14\t核心转变：不再主张任何 formulation 普遍更好，而是 characterize 何时用什么。\n15\t最强贡献重新定位：\n16\t1. CWM 失败模式是 **tokenizer/model-specific** 而非 formulation-inherent（Qwen 93% unparseable vs DeepSeek 11.8%）\n17\t2. Error complementarity: CLS/CWM 有系统性互补错误模式，oracle ensemble +2-3pp\n18\t3. 复杂度是 formulation 选择的关键维度（func-level 等价，repo-level 分化）\n19\t\n20\t## Core Claims (revised per D116)\n21\t\n22\t1. **Formulation Equivalence at Low Complexity**: At function-level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ achieve statistically equivalent accuracy across two model families (Qwen3: 88.4/87.2/86.3%; DeepSeek: 86.9/86.8/84.2%). Formulation choice does not matter when execution outputs are short and structured.\n23\t\n24\t2. **Complexity-Dependent Divergence (Model-Contingent)**: At repo-level, formulation effectiveness depends on model/tokenizer properties:\n25\t   - Qwen3: CLS dominates CWM by 19-26pp due to 54-93% unparseable rate (tokenizer-specific CWM collapse)\n26\t   - DeepSeek: ⏳ **PENDING** — results determine narrative direction:\n27\t     - If CLS > CWM: \"complexity-dependent advantage is consistent across model families\"\n28\t     - If CWM ≥ CLS: \"advantage is model/tokenizer-contingent; CWM works when tokenizer supports structured generation\"\n29\t   - Either outcome supports the design space characterization framing\n30\t\n31\t3. **Diagnostic Granularity Without Accuracy Cost**: Per-test CLS achieves TOST equivalence with trajectory-level scoring (p=0.007, ±2pp margin, Qwen3) while providing per-test failure localization. Efficiency advantage: 6-9x inference speedup, 8x batch capacity on 24GB GPU.\n32\t\n33\t## Story Spine (D116 revision)\n34\t\n35\t**Problem**: Execution-free verification for code repair can be formulated in multiple ways (per-test classification, execution output generation, trajectory-level scoring), but no systematic comparison exists. Practitioners lack guidance on which formulation to use under what conditions.\n36\t\n37\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Code World Models generate execution outputs but suffer from format compliance failures at scale. Trajectory-level verifiers (SWE-RM) provide coarse binary signals without per-test diagnostics. Classification-based verifiers (LEVER, CodeT) rank candidates but don't provide per-test failure localization. No work provides a controlled comparison across these formulations holding model, data, and compute constant.\n38\t\n39\t**Our contribution**: We present the first controlled comparison of three verification formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) across 2 model families, 2 complexity levels, and multiple seeds. Key findings:\n40\t1. Formulations are equivalent at function-level (null result establishing baseline)\n41\t2. Formulations diverge at repo-level in a model-contingent manner\n42\t3. CWM failure at repo-level is tokenizer-specific (not formulation-inherent): unparseable rate drops from 93% (Qwen) to [X]% (DeepSeek)\n43\t4. CLS and CWM exhibit complementary error patterns (oracle ensemble: 90.63%)\n44\t5. Per-test CLS matches trajectory-level accuracy while providing diagnostic granularity at 6-9x lower inference cost\n45\t\n46\t**Headline result template (dual-path)**:\n47\t- Path A (CLS > CWM on DeepSeek): \"Classification consistently outperforms generation at repo-level across model families, but the magnitude depends on tokenizer-specific format compliance. We characterize when and why each formulation succeeds.\"\n48\t- Path B (CWM ≥ CLS on DeepSeek): \"No single formulation dominates: CLS wins on Qwen (tokenizer-induced CWM collapse) while CWM matches/exceeds CLS on DeepSeek. The formulation design space is model-contingent, and we provide the empirical characterization needed to navigate it.\"\n49\t\n50\t## Venue Fit Risks\n51\t\n52\t1. **Novelty concern (Dream consensus)**: \"Classification > generation when outputs are complex\" is predictable. Mitigation: novelty is in (a) empirical demonstration that it's tokenizer-specific not formulation-inherent, (b) error complementarity analysis, (c) systematic controlled comparison methodology. Frame as \"empirical characterization with actionable insights\" not \"method contribution.\"\n53\t\n54\t2. **EMNLP vs SE venue**: Mitigation: (a) process vs outcome supervision parallel (Lightman et al., 2023; Uesato et al., 2022), (b) general NLP methodology insight about classification vs generation.\n55\t\n56\t3. **CWM comparison fairness**: Original CWM is 32B with mid-training on execution traces; we compare 4-8B LoRA. Mitigation: explicitly scope as \"same-size LoRA comparison\" and discuss that generation may need more capacity. This limitation actually strengthens the practical guidance: \"at practical deployment sizes (4-8B), classification is the safer choice.\"\n57\t\n58\t4. **Re-repair null result**: Downstream utility unvalidated. Mitigation: frame efficiency + diagnostic granularity as the practical benefit, not re-repair. Re-repair is future work.\n59\t\n60\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigations (updated per Dream)\n61\t\n62\t| Concern | Mitigation |\n63\t|---------|------------|\n64\t| \"Limited novelty — obvious that classification is easier\" | Func-level null result proves it's NOT trivially easier; advantage is complexity+tokenizer-dependent. Strongest novelty: CWM failure is tokenizer-specific |\n65\t| \"CWM comparison unfair (4-8B LoRA vs 32B full)\" | Explicitly scope as same-size comparison; discuss scale as limitation; practical guidance framing |\n66\t| \"Single-seed repo-level\" | Multi-seed replication (2 seeds × 2 formulations × DeepSeek, running) |\n67\t| \"Cross-model validation incomplete\" | DeepSeek repo experiments (running); whichever direction supports the design space characterization |\n68\t| \"No downstream utility\" | Efficiency benefit (6-9x) is practical; re-repair honestly framed as future work |\n69\t| \"Claims outrun evidence\" | D116: remove all advocacy language; report what evidence supports, nothing more |\n70\t| \"Process vs outcome supervision parallel\" | Add Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 to Related Work |\n71\t\n72\t## Related Work Additions Needed (Dream feedback)\n73\t- Process vs outcome supervision: Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 (CLS vs TRAJ parallel)\n74\t- CodeRL, AlphaCode, Reflexion (verification-in-the-loop repair)\n75\t- Predictive mutation testing literature (per-test binary classification precedent)\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36c9cf1b-ce10-4bcf-a0f9-441195ff84d5","uuid":"8a9d2a4e-bd82-4030-94ea-c076da5ca0df","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:42:10.599Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T171503/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — exec-sim-repair-verifier\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Extended fallback: ICSE 2027 (Jun 23 abstract, Jun 30 paper)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (9 days remaining)\n\n## D116 Framing Pivot (2026-05-16)\n\n**前 framing**: \"CLS scales where generation fails\" (CLS advocacy)\n**新 framing**: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n\n核心转变：不再主张任何 formulation 普遍更好，而是 characterize 何时用什么。\n最强贡献重新定位：\n1. CWM 失败模式是 **tokenizer/model-specific** 而非 formulation-inherent（Qwen 93% unparseable vs DeepSeek 11.8%）\n2. Error complementarity: CLS/CWM 有系统性互补错误模式，oracle ensemble +2-3pp\n3. 复杂度是 formulation 选择的关键维度（func-level 等价，repo-level 分化）\n\n## Core Claims (revised per D116)\n\n1. **Formulation Equivalence at Low Complexity**: At function-level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ achieve statistically equivalent accuracy across two model families (Qwen3: 88.4/87.2/86.3%; DeepSeek: 86.9/86.8/84.2%). Formulation choice does not matter when execution outputs are short and structured.\n\n2. **Complexity-Dependent Divergence (Model-Contingent)**: At repo-level, formulation effectiveness depends on model/tokenizer properties:\n   - Qwen3: CLS dominates CWM by 19-26pp due to 54-93% unparseable rate (tokenizer-specific CWM collapse)\n   - DeepSeek: ⏳ **PENDING** — results determine narrative direction:\n     - If CLS > CWM: \"complexity-dependent advantage is consistent across model families\"\n     - If CWM ≥ CLS: \"advantage is model/tokenizer-contingent; CWM works when tokenizer supports structured generation\"\n   - Either outcome supports the design space characterization framing\n\n3. **Diagnostic Granularity Without Accuracy Cost**: Per-test CLS achieves TOST equivalence with trajectory-level scoring (p=0.007, ±2pp margin, Qwen3) while providing per-test failure localization. Efficiency advantage: 6-9x inference speedup, 8x batch capacity on 24GB GPU.\n\n## Story Spine (D116 revision)\n\n**Problem**: Execution-free verification for code repair can be formulated in multiple ways (per-test classification, execution output generation, trajectory-level scoring), but no systematic comparison exists. Practitioners lack guidance on which formulation to use under what conditions.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Code World Models generate execution outputs but suffer from format compliance failures at scale. Trajectory-level verifiers (SWE-RM) provide coarse binary signals without per-test diagnostics. Classification-based verifiers (LEVER, CodeT) rank candidates but don't provide per-test failure localization. No work provides a controlled comparison across these formulations holding model, data, and compute constant.\n\n**Our contribution**: We present the first controlled comparison of three verification formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) across 2 model families, 2 complexity levels, and multiple seeds. Key findings:\n1. Formulations are equivalent at function-level (null result establishing baseline)\n2. Formulations diverge at repo-level in a model-contingent manner\n3. CWM failure at repo-level is tokenizer-specific (not formulation-inherent): unparseable rate drops from 93% (Qwen) to [X]% (DeepSeek)\n4. CLS and CWM exhibit complementary error patterns (oracle ensemble: 90.63%)\n5. Per-test CLS matches trajectory-level accuracy while providing diagnostic granularity at 6-9x lower inference cost\n\n**Headline result template (dual-path)**:\n- Path A (CLS > CWM on DeepSeek): \"Classification consistently outperforms generation at repo-level across model families, but the magnitude depends on tokenizer-specific format compliance. We characterize when and why each formulation succeeds.\"\n- Path B (CWM ≥ CLS on DeepSeek): \"No single formulation dominates: CLS wins on Qwen (tokenizer-induced CWM collapse) while CWM matches/exceeds CLS on DeepSeek. The formulation design space is model-contingent, and we provide the empirical characterization needed to navigate it.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n1. **Novelty concern (Dream consensus)**: \"Classification > generation when outputs are complex\" is predictable. Mitigation: novelty is in (a) empirical demonstration that it's tokenizer-specific not formulation-inherent, (b) error complementarity analysis, (c) systematic controlled comparison methodology. Frame as \"empirical characterization with actionable insights\" not \"method contribution.\"\n\n2. **EMNLP vs SE venue**: Mitigation: (a) process vs outcome supervision parallel (Lightman et al., 2023; Uesato et al., 2022), (b) general NLP methodology insight about classification vs generation.\n\n3. **CWM comparison fairness**: Original CWM is 32B with mid-training on execution traces; we compare 4-8B LoRA. Mitigation: explicitly scope as \"same-size LoRA comparison\" and discuss that generation may need more capacity. This limitation actually strengthens the practical guidance: \"at practical deployment sizes (4-8B), classification is the safer choice.\"\n\n4. **Re-repair null result**: Downstream utility unvalidated. Mitigation: frame efficiency + diagnostic granularity as the practical benefit, not re-repair. Re-repair is future work.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigations (updated per Dream)\n\n| Concern | Mitigation |\n|---------|------------|\n| \"Limited novelty — obvious that classification is easier\" | Func-level null result proves it's NOT trivially easier; advantage is complexity+tokenizer-dependent. Strongest novelty: CWM failure is tokenizer-specific |\n| \"CWM comparison unfair (4-8B LoRA vs 32B full)\" | Explicitly scope as same-size comparison; discuss scale as limitation; practical guidance framing |\n| \"Single-seed repo-level\" | Multi-seed replication (2 seeds × 2 formulations × DeepSeek, running) |\n| \"Cross-model validation incomplete\" | DeepSeek repo experiments (running); whichever direction supports the design space characterization |\n| \"No downstream utility\" | Efficiency benefit (6-9x) is practical; re-repair honestly framed as future work |\n| \"Claims outrun evidence\" | D116: remove all advocacy language; report what evidence supports, nothing more |\n| \"Process vs outcome supervision parallel\" | Add Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 to Related Work |\n\n## Related Work Additions Needed (Dream feedback)\n- Process vs outcome supervision: Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 (CLS vs TRAJ parallel)\n- CodeRL, AlphaCode, Reflexion (verification-in-the-loop repair)\n- Predictive mutation testing literature (per-test binary classification precedent)\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WSZE94kBqEu2Lt99ogXRaQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"CWM Generation Baseline (Qwen3-4B)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B LoRA CWM 生成 baseline，预测 execution output 而非 pass/fail\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"overall_accuracy\": 87.51,\n7\t      \"pass_f1\": 87.31,\n8\t      \"fail_f1\": 87.71,\n9\t      \"exact_match_rate\": 84.02,\n10\t      \"unparseable_predictions\": 0\n11\t    },\n12\t    \"tables\": [\n13\t      \"Table 2: Func-level formulation comparison\"\n14\t    ],\n15\t    \"figures\": [],\n16\t    \"analysis\": \"func-level CWM=CLS 是 worst tier 的基础支撑——证明 formulation 选择在低复杂度下不重要，\\n这是一个有 statistical backing 的 null result（TOST p=0.007）。\\n\\n\\nFunc-level execution output 短且结构化（通常 <50 tokens），Qwen3-4B 能完美解析。\\nCWM 与 CLS 在 func-level 本质上等价：CWM 先生成 output 再隐式比较，CLS 直接二分类，\\n当 output 空间小时两者信息量一致。87.51% 与 CLS seed42 的 87.83% 在噪声范围内。\\n\"\n17\t  },\n18\t  {\n19\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed Core Comparison (CLS vs CWM vs TRAJ, Qwen3-4B)\",\n20\t    \"description\": \"CLS/CWM 各 5 seeds + TRAJ 4 seeds 的 func-level 多种子验证\",\n21\t    \"results\": {\n22\t      \"cls_4b_mean_acc\": 88.43,\n23\t      \"cls_4b_std\": 0.73,\n24\t      \"cls_4b_seeds\": {\n25\t        \"s42\": 87.83,\n26\t        \"s123\": 89.52,\n27\t        \"s456\": 87.88,\n28\t        \"s789\": 89.0,\n29\t        \"s0\": 87.94\n30\t      },\n31\t      \"cwm_4b_mean_acc\": 87.19,\n32\t      \"cwm_4b_std\": 0.37,\n33\t      \"cwm_4b_seeds\": {\n34\t        \"s42\": 87.51,\n35\t        \"s123\": 87.2,\n36\t        \"s456\": 86.98,\n37\t        \"s789\": 86.67,\n38\t        \"s0\": 87.57\n39\t      },\n40\t      \"traj_4b_mean_acc\": 86.46,\n41\t      \"traj_4b_std\": 1.01,\n42\t      \"traj_4b_seeds\": {\n43\t        \"s0\": 85.66,\n44\t        \"s123\": 85.47,\n45\t        \"s456\": 87.4,\n46\t        \"s789\": 87.31\n47\t      },\n48\t      \"pooled_cls_cwm_gap_pp\": -0.45,\n49\t      \"tost_p_value\": 0.0071,\n50\t      \"tost_margin_pp\": 2.0,\n51\t      \"cls_vs_traj_gap_pp\": 1.97\n52\t    },\n53\t    \"tables\": [\n54\t      \"Table 2: Func-level formulation comparison\",\n55\t      \"Table 3: Multi-seed statistics\"\n56\t    ],\n57\t    \"figures\": [],\n58\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 paper 最 solid 的 statistical result。TOST p=0.007 是 reviewer 难以反驳的。\\n但 novelty concern 在于：func-level 等价本身是 predictable 的（output 短 → 生成不难）。\\n\\n\\n5-seed CLS 和 CWM 的 pooled gap 仅 0.45pp（CWM 略高），TOST 等价检验 p=0.007 在\\n±2pp margin 内确认统计等价。TRAJ 略低 ~2pp 但方差更大（std=1.01 vs 0.73/0.37），\\n反映 trajectory-level aggregation 引入的 problem-level 随机性。三种 formulation\\n在 func-level 的差异不具有实际意义。\\n\"\n59\t  },\n60\t  {\n61\t    \"name\": \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation (Qwen3-4B)\",\n62\t    \"description\": \"Chain-of-thought 式先推理后判断，测试显式 execution reasoning 是否有帮助\",\n63\t    \"results\": {\n64\t      \"conclusion\": \"failed\",\n65\t      \"training_outcome\": \"模型未能学会生成有意义的 execution trace，输出退化为模板化文本\"\n66\t    },\n67\t    \"tables\": [],\n68\t    \"figures\": [],\n69\t    \"analysis\": \"负面结果但有叙事价值：证明 \\\"更多推理步骤\\\" 在小模型 + LoRA 场景下不一定有帮助，\\n支持直接分类的 simplicity argument。在 worst tier 下降为 footnote。\\n\\n\\n4B LoRA 容量不足以同时学习 execution reasoning 和 pass/fail 判断。Trace 生成\\n引入了额外的 teacher-forcing 误差累积，且训练数据中没有 ground-truth trace 作为监督。\\n模型要么忽略 trace 直接跳到 label（使 trace 无意义），要么在 trace 阶段积累错误\\n导致最终判断变差。\\n\"\n70\t  },\n71\t  {\n72\t    \"name\": \"Trajectory-level Finetuned Baseline (Qwen3-4B)\",\n73\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B LoRA trajectory-level verifier (resolved/unresolved)\",\n74\t    \"results\": {\n75\t      \"accuracy\": 85.66,\n76\t      \"unresolved_f1\": 87.5,\n77\t      \"resolved_f1\": 83.18,\n78\t      \"per_test_consistency\": 79.94\n79\t    },\n80\t    \"tables\": [\n81\t      \"Table 2\"\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"CLS vs TRAJ 的 ~2pp 差距支持 \\\"per-test 粒度不损失精度\\\" 的 claim。但 worst tier\\n下这个差距在 multi-seed 中有时反转（seed456 TRAJ=87.4% > CLS=87.88% 差距仅 0.48pp），\\n需要依赖 TOST 而非 point estimate 来论证。\\n\\n\\nTrajectory-level 将多个 test 聚合为单一 resolved/unresolved 标签，丢失了 per-test\\n粒度信息。85.66% accuracy 低于 per-test CLS 的 88.43% mean，差异来自 aggregation\\n信息损失——当一个 problem 有 n 个 test 时，trajectory 模型需要从更长的拼接 input\\n中做出单一判断，而 CLS 可以独立判断每个 test。per_test_consistency=79.94% 表明\\n约 20% 的 per-test 判断与 trajectory 结论不一致。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"Model Size Scaling (Qwen3-8B CLS vs CWM)\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"8B 模型规模下的 CLS vs CWM 对比\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"cls_8b_mean_acc\": 89.39,\n91\t      \"cls_8b_seeds\": {\n92\t        \"s42\": 90.48,\n93\t        \"s123\": 89.37,\n94\t        \"s456\": 88.31\n95\t      },\n96\t      \"cwm_8b_mean_acc\": 86.96,\n97\t      \"cwm_8b_seeds\": {\n98\t        \"s42\": 87.67,\n99\t        \"s123\": 86.98,\n100\t        \"s456\": 86.24\n101\t      },\n102\t      \"cls_8b_vs_cwm_8b_gap_pp\": 2.43,\n103\t      \"cls_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp\": 0.96,\n104\t      \"cwm_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp\": -0.23\n105\t    },\n106\t    \"tables\": [\n107\t      \"Table 2\"\n108\t    ],\n109\t    \"figures\": [],\n110\t    \"analysis\": \"8B CLS > CWM 的 gap 比 4B 更明显，但仍然在 func-level。这个结果在所有 tier 共享，\\nworst tier 下支持 \\\"scaling 不帮助 CWM\\\" 的 finding。\\n\\n\\nCLS 从 4B→8B 提升约 1pp（88.43→89.39%），CWM 几乎不变（87.19→86.96%，甚至略降）。\\n这表明 CWM 的瓶颈不在模型容量而在 formulation 本身——生成 exact output 的 ceiling\\n由 exact_match 约束决定，更大模型不能突破。CLS 因为是 binary classification 任务，\\n更大模型的 representation capacity 能略微提升边界样本的判断。8B 规模下 CLS 首次\\n明确超过 CWM（2.43pp gap，超出 multi-seed 噪声范围）。\\n\"\n111\t  },\n112\t  {\n113\t    \"name\": \"LLM Judge Zero-shot Baseline (Qwen3-8B/32B)\",\n114\t    \"description\": \"零样本 LLM-as-judge 基线，per-test + trajectory-level\",\n115\t    \"results\": {\n116\t      \"per_test_8b_acc\": 64.4,\n117\t      \"per_test_32b_acc\": 71.69,\n118\t      \"majority_baseline\": 51.75,\n119\t      \"traj_8b_acc\": 99.1,\n120\t      \"traj_32b_acc\": 99.12,\n121\t      \"traj_8b_true_resolved\": 1,\n122\t      \"traj_8b_pred_resolved\": 0\n123\t    },\n124\t    \"tables\": [\n125\t      \"Table 2: as baseline row\"\n126\t    ],\n127\t    \"figures\": [],\n128\t    \"analysis\": \"Fine-tuned vs zero-shot 的巨大 gap（87% vs 64-72%）证明 task-specific training\\n的必要性。Zero-shot TRAJ 的 99.1%（=majority baseline）是 cautionary result。\\n\\n\\nPer-test 零样本表现远低于 fine-tuned（64-72% vs 87-90%），因为模型需要理解\\nmutation 引入的 subtle 错误并预测 test 行为，而非简单的 pattern matching。\\nTrajectory-level 99.1% 是虚假高分——模型几乎总是预测 \\\"unresolved\\\"，在 114 个\\nproblem 中只有 1 个是 resolved，majority baseline 就是 99.1%。这暴露了零样本\\ntrajectory-level 评估在极度 imbalanced 场景下的无效性。\\n\"\n129\t  },\n130\t  {\n131\t    \"name\": \"Per-test Majority Voting (K=3)\",\n132\t    \"description\": \"Self-consistency 多数投票，测试 K=3 采样是否提升准确率\",\n133\t    \"results\": {\n134\t      \"accuracy_greedy\": 87.51,\n135\t      \"accuracy_majority_vote\": 86.83,\n136\t      \"delta_pp\": -0.69,\n137\t      \"net_flips\": -13,\n138\t      \"wall_time_ratio\": 4.0\n139\t    },\n140\t    \"tables\": [],\n141\t    \"figures\": [],\n142\t    \"analysis\": \"负面结果。排除了一个简单的 improvement avenue，但不影响核心叙事。\\n在 worst tier 下可以放入 appendix 或完全省略。\\n\\n\\nGreedy decoding 在 classification 任务上已接近模型能力上限。K=3 采样引入的随机性\\n对 high-confidence 正确预测无帮助，反而对 low-confidence 边界样本引入噪声：\\n28 个正确→错误 vs 15 个错误→正确 = net -13 flips。CLS 的 decision boundary 是\\ndeterministic 的（logit > 0 → pass），temperature sampling 只会模糊这个边界。\\n这与 generation 任务（如 code generation）中 majority voting 有效不同。\\n\"\n143\t  },\n144\t  {\n145\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek Func-level Cross-model Validation (CLS + CWM + TRAJ)\",\n146\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上重复 func-level 三种 formulation 对比\",\n147\t    \"results\": {\n148\t      \"deepseek_cls_mean\": 86.85,\n149\t      \"deepseek_cls_seeds\": {\n150\t        \"s42\": 86.93,\n151\t        \"s123\": 86.77\n152\t      },\n153\t      \"deepseek_cwm_mean\": 86.83,\n154\t      \"deepseek_cwm_seeds\": {\n155\t        \"s42\": 85.77,\n156\t        \"s123\": 87.88\n157\t      },\n158\t      \"deepseek_traj_mean\": 84.16,\n159\t      \"deepseek_traj_seeds\": {\n160\t        \"v2\": 83.24,\n161\t        \"v2_s123\": 85.08\n162\t      },\n163\t      \"deepseek_cwm_unparseable_rate\": 0.0,\n164\t      \"cross_model_cls_cwm_gap_pp\": 0.02,\n165\t      \"cross_model_cls_traj_gap_pp\": 2.69\n166\t    },\n167\t    \"tables\": [\n168\t      \"Table 2: DeepSeek rows\"\n169\t    ],\n170\t    \"figures\": [],\n171\t    \"analysis\": \"Func-level 双模型族验证完整且 clean。CLS≈CWM 在两个模型族都成立。\\n这是 worst tier 最强的跨模型证据，但 reviewer 会认为 func-level 等价本身 novelty 低。\\n\\n\\nDeepSeek func-level 重现了 Qwen 的 pattern：CLS≈CWM（86.85 vs 86.83%，gap 0.02pp），\\nTRAJ 略低（84.16%，gap ~2.7pp）。注意 DeepSeek CWM unparseable=0%，与 Qwen CWM\\nfunc-level 一致——func-level output 足够短，两种 tokenizer 都能完美解析。\\nDeepSeek TRAJ 比 Qwen TRAJ 低 ~2pp，可能因为 DeepSeek-Coder 的 instruction-following\\n能力在 trajectory aggregation 场景下略弱。\\n\"\n172\t  },\n173\t  {\n174\t    \"name\": \"Per-test Failure Prediction Precision/Recall\",\n175\t    \"description\": \"Per-test 粒度的 failure 预测精度分析\",\n176\t    \"results\": {\n177\t      \"accuracy\": 87.51,\n178\t      \"fail_precision\": 82.75,\n179\t      \"fail_recall\": 93.64,\n180\t      \"fail_f1\": 87.86,\n181\t      \"best_mutation\": \"return_value (97.26%)\",\n182\t      \"worst_mutation\": \"off_by_one (82.56%)\"\n183\t    },\n184\t    \"tables\": [\n185\t      \"Table 5: Per-test diagnostic quality\"\n186\t    ],\n187\t    \"figures\": [],\n188\t    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic granularity 分析完整。但没有 downstream 验证（re-repair 为负），\\nworst tier 下只能声称 \\\"potentially useful for debugging\\\" 而非 \\\"proven useful\\\"。\\n\\n\\nHigh recall (93.64%) 意味着模型捕获了绝大多数真实 failure，但 precision (82.75%)\\n说明约 17% 的 failure 预测是误报。这在 diagnostic 场景下是可接受的——宁可多报\\nfailure 也不要漏掉（fail-safe 偏好）。Mutation type 分析显示 return_value mutations\\n最容易检测（明显的输出差异），off_by_one 最难（微妙的边界差异）。\\n\"\n189\t  },\n190\t  {\n191\t    \"name\": \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\",\n192\t    \"description\": \"按 failing test 数量分层的 oracle advantage 分析\",\n193\t    \"results\": {\n194\t      \"T1_pct\": 68.7,\n195\t      \"T1_block_adv\": -0.09,\n196\t      \"T2_pct\": 19.1,\n197\t      \"T2_block_adv\": 31.69,\n198\t      \"T3_5_block_adv\": 40.74,\n199\t      \"T6plus_block_adv\": 40.06,\n200\t      \"overall_block_adv\": 10.93,\n201\t      \"T2_contribution_pct\": 55.3\n202\t    },\n203\t    \"tables\": [\n204\t      \"Table 6\"\n205\t    ],\n206\t    \"figures\": [],\n207\t    \"analysis\": \"Oracle analysis 显示 per-test 的理论优势存在但受限于 T=1 dominance。\\nWorst tier 下 reviewer 会指出 \\\"68.7% 的 instances per-test 不提供额外信息\\\"。\\n\\n\\n68.7% 的 instances 只有 1 个 failing test (T=1)，此时 per-test 和 trajectory-level\\n信息等价（只有一个 test 决定成败）。Per-test 优势集中在 T≥2（31.5% 的 instances），\\n其中 T=2 贡献了 55.3% 的总 advantage。这是因为 T=2 时 per-test 能区分 \\\"一个 test fail\\\"\\nvs \\\"两个 test fail\\\" 而 trajectory 只能说 \\\"unresolved\\\"。T≥3 的 advantage 更大但\\ninstance 更少。SWE-bench 的 median F2P=1 限制了 per-test 的 practical impact。\\n\"\n208\t  },\n209\t  {\n210\t    \"name\": \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\",\n211\t    \"description\": \"验证 per-test predictions 的 intra-problem 相关性结构\",\n212\t    \"results\": {\n213\t      \"icc\": 0.1909,\n214\t      \"icc_p_value\": 0.0,\n215\t      \"design_effect\": 3.9676,\n216\t      \"all_correct_observed\": 46,\n217\t      \"all_correct_expected_iid\": 16.35,\n218\t      \"all_correct_ratio\": 2.81\n219\t    },\n220\t    \"tables\": [\n221\t      \"Table 7: Block correlation analysis\"\n222\t    ],\n223\t    \"figures\": [],\n224\t    \"analysis\": \"这是一个 methodological contribution：揭示 per-test evaluation 中 i.i.d. 假设\\n不成立，标准 CI 会低估 variance。ICC=0.19 + DE=3.97 是 clean statistical result。\\nWorst tier 下这可能是最独特的贡献——之前没有工作量化过 per-test verification 中的\\nintra-problem correlation。但 reviewer 可能认为这更适合 statistics 会议。\\n\\n\\nICC=0.19 表明同一 problem 内的 per-test 预测错误有显著相关性（p<0.001），\\ndesign effect=3.97 意味着 effective sample size 约为 nominal 的 1/4。\\nObserved all-correct rate (46/114=40.4%) 远高于 i.i.d. 预期 (14.3%)，\\nratio=2.81 说明模型错误在 problem 内是 clustered 的——要么全对，要么错多个。\\n这挑战了 per-test evaluation 中常见的 i.i.d. 假设。\\n\"\n225\t  },\n226\t  {\n227\t    \"name\": \"Oracle Total (F2P+P2P) Validated\",\n228\t    \"description\": \"包含 P2P regression tests 的 oracle advantage 验证\",\n229\t    \"results\": {\n230\t      \"total_reg5pct_block_adv\": -0.005,\n231\t      \"total_reg10pct_block_adv\": 0.083,\n232\t      \"total_reg20pct_block_adv\": 0.278,\n233\t      \"total_reg5pct_pass\": false,\n234\t      \"total_reg10pct_pass\": true\n235\t    },\n236\t    \"tables\": [\n237\t      \"Table 6 extended\"\n238\t    ],\n239\t    \"figures\": [],\n240\t    \"analysis\": \"P2P 在低 regression rate 下无帮助甚至有害。Worst tier 下这个发现缩窄了 per-test\\n的 applicable scope，reviewer 会用这个来质疑 practical significance。\\n\\n\\nP2P regression rate ≤5% 时 per-test advantage 消失（-0.5pp），因为 P2P tests\\n几乎全 pass，不提供 discriminative 信息。只有 regression rate ≥10% 时 per-test\\n才有正 advantage。实际 regression rate 通常 <5%（高质量修复），这意味着\\nper-test 的优势主要在 F2P tests 上，P2P tests 是 noise source。\\n\"\n241\t  },\n242\t  {\n243\t    \"name\": \"Repo-level CLS (Qwen3-4B, best checkpoint)\",\n244\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B LoRA repo-level classification，最优 checkpoint 评估\",\n245\t    \"results\": {\n246\t      \"best_checkpoint\": \"ckpt-4600\",\n247\t      \"test_accuracy\": 83.63,\n248\t      \"test_f1_macro\": 75.63,\n249\t      \"test_fail_f1\": 61.67,\n250\t      \"test_pass_f1\": 89.59,\n251\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n252\t      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": 10.67,\n253\t      \"val_accuracy\": 90.07,\n254\t      \"val_test_gap_pp\": 6.44\n255\t    },\n256\t    \"tables\": [\n257\t      \"Table 4: Repo-level comparison\"\n258\t    ],\n259\t    \"figures\": [],\n260\t    \"analysis\": \"83.63% 在 worst tier 范围 [83, 86] 的下端。只有 Qwen 一个模型族达到这个水平，\\nreviewer 会质疑 generalizability。\\n\\n\\nRepo-level CLS 在 Qwen3-4B 上达到 83.63% test accuracy，显著超过 majority baseline\\n10.67pp。但 val-test gap 高达 6.44pp 暴露了 overfitting 或 distribution shift。\\nFail_f1 仅 61.67%（vs func-level 88%），说明 repo-level 的长 context + 复杂依赖\\n大幅增加了分类难度。这是 worst tier Qwen repo-level 的 reference point。\\n\"\n261\t  },\n262\t  {\n263\t    \"name\": \"Repo-level CLS (Qwen3-8B, best configurations)\",\n264\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B LoRA repo-level classification，多 seed 多 checkpoint\",\n265\t    \"results\": {\n266\t      \"best_s42_ckpt\": \"ckpt-400\",\n267\t      \"best_s42_test_acc\": 84.79,\n268\t      \"best_s123_ckpt\": \"ckpt-3000\",\n269\t      \"best_s123_test_acc\": 85.6,\n270\t      \"best_s123_val_acc\": 88.69,\n271\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96\n272\t    },\n273\t    \"tables\": [\n274\t      \"Table 4\"\n275\t    ],\n276\t    \"figures\": [],\n277\t    \"analysis\": \"85.60% 是 Qwen repo-level CLS 的 ceiling。但 checkpoint 选择的高度敏感性\\n削弱了结果的可靠性。Worst tier 下 reviewer 会质问 \\\"你怎么选 checkpoint\\\"。\\n\\n\\n8B 比 4B 提升 1-2pp（84.79/85.60 vs 83.63），但 s42 和 s123 的 best checkpoint\\n差异巨大（ckpt-400 vs ckpt-3000），暗示 repo-level 训练对 seed 和 checkpoint\\n选择极度敏感。Overfitting 严重——s42 继续训练到 ckpt-1000+ 后 accuracy 反而\\n下降到 83-84%。这种 instability 是 reviewer concern 的来源。\\n\"\n278\t  },\n279\t  {\n280\t    \"name\": \"Repo-level CWM (Qwen, all versions)\",\n281\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3 repo-level CWM generation，v3-v12 全部尝试\",\n282\t    \"results\": {\n283\t      \"v10_accuracy\": 69.91,\n284\t      \"v10_unparseable_pct\": 93.0,\n285\t      \"v11_accuracy\": 66.6,\n286\t      \"v11_unparseable_pct\": 75.2,\n287\t      \"v12_accuracy\": 58.04,\n288\t      \"v12_unparseable_pct\": 53.7,\n289\t      \"best_parseable_accuracy\": \"~42-58% (估计)\",\n290\t      \"all_versions_below_majority\": true\n291\t    },\n292\t    \"tables\": [\n293\t      \"Table 4: CWM row\"\n294\t    ],\n295\t    \"figures\": [],\n296\t    \"analysis\": \"CWM repo-level 在 Qwen 上彻底失败。Worst tier 下无法报告有意义的 CWM repo accuracy，\\n只能报告 unparseable rate 作为 negative finding。但这反而支持 \\\"CWM failure 是\\ntokenizer-specific\\\" 的 claim——如果 DeepSeek CWM repo 也失败（worst tier 假设），\\n则需要修改为 \\\"CWM repo failure 可能是 formulation-inherent at small model scale\\\"。\\n\\n\\nQwen tokenizer 在 repo-level 长 output 生成中灾难性失败。v10（max_new_tokens=64）\\n93% unparseable——token budget 太小无法生成完整 execution output。放宽到更大 budget\\n后 v12 unparseable 降到 53.7% 但 accuracy 更差（58%）——模型在长生成中 drift。\\nQwen3 的 tokenizer 对结构化 execution output 的 token 效率极低，是 model-specific\\nfailure 而非 formulation-inherent failure。\\n\"\n297\t  },\n298\t  {\n299\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-level v5 (seed42, full 3 epochs)\",\n300\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B repo-level CLS，v5 完整 3 epoch 训练\",\n301\t    \"results\": {\n302\t      \"training_outcome\": \"完成但 acc 未超过 majority baseline\",\n303\t      \"test_accuracy\": 71.5,\n304\t      \"f1_macro\": 54.2,\n305\t      \"f1_fail\": 28.3,\n306\t      \"f1_pass\": 80.1,\n307\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n308\t      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": -1.46,\n309\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.01,\n310\t      \"confusion_pattern\": \"严重偏向预测 pass，recall_fail < 20%\"\n311\t    },\n312\t    \"tables\": [\n313\t      \"Table 4: DeepSeek CLS row — 标注为 ≈baseline 或 below baseline\"\n314\t    ],\n315\t    \"figures\": [],\n316\t    \"analysis\": \"DeepSeek CLS repo v1-v5 全部失败。s123 的 74.93% 是唯一勉强高于 baseline 的数据点，\\n但 f1_fail=22.84% 说明模型几乎不能识别 failure（几乎全预测 pass）。\\nWorst tier 叙事：DeepSeek repo-level CLS 不可用，repo-level 比较仅限 Qwen。\\n\\n\\nv4（2 epoch 不完整）eval_loss=NaN 所有 epoch，process killed。v5 是 v4 的完整重跑。\\nv4 已有的 ckpt-200 eval（71.37% acc）低于 majority baseline。s123 的完整训练\\n也只达到 74.93%（勉强高于 73% baseline），且 recall_fail=13.72% 几乎不识别 fail。\\nDeepSeek-Coder 在 repo-level 的核心问题：(1) max_seq_length=2048 对 repo context\\n截断过多（平均 repo input ~5000 tokens），丢失关键依赖信息；(2) 6.7B LoRA 容量\\n不足以学习 repo-level 的复杂 pass/fail pattern；(3) eval_loss=NaN 暗示训练不稳定，\\n3 epoch 可能过拟合或 loss landscape 有 pathological region。\\nWorst tier 预测 v5 在 70-73% 范围，不超过 majority baseline。\\n\"\n317\t  },\n318\t  {\n319\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-level s123 (seed123)\",\n320\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B repo-level CLS seed=123 的评估结果\",\n321\t    \"results\": {\n322\t      \"test_accuracy\": 74.93,\n323\t      \"f1_macro\": 53.94,\n324\t      \"f1_fail\": 22.84,\n325\t      \"f1_pass\": 85.03,\n326\t      \"recall_fail\": 13.72,\n327\t      \"recall_pass\": 97.62,\n328\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n329\t      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": 1.97\n330\t    },\n331\t    \"tables\": [\n332\t      \"Table 4\"\n333\t    ],\n334\t    \"figures\": [],\n335\t    \"analysis\": \"这个结果已经 confirm worst-tier 假设。DeepSeek CLS repo essentially at majority baseline。\\nCombined with v5 prediction, worst tier 叙事完全成立。\\n\\n\\n74.93% 仅比 majority baseline 高 1.97pp。F1_fail=22.84% 揭示模型几乎完全\\ncollapse 到 majority class (pass)：recall_fail=13.72% 意味着 86% 的真实 failure\\n被误判为 pass。这不是一个有用的分类器——一个简单的 \\\"always predict pass\\\" baseline\\n就能达到 73%。Gap 1.97pp 在 multi-seed 噪声范围内不可靠。\\n\"\n336\t  },\n337\t  {\n338\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-level s42 Epoch 3 (canonical seq2048)\",\n339\t    \"description\": \"D131: DeepSeek CWM repo s42 epoch 3 在 canonical seq2048 下的评估\",\n340\t    \"results\": {\n341\t      \"test_accuracy\": 52.3,\n342\t      \"f1_macro\": 44.8,\n343\t      \"f1_fail\": 18.5,\n344\t      \"f1_pass\": 71.1,\n345\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 82.0,\n346\t      \"unparseable_count\": 8023,\n347\t      \"parseable_only_accuracy\": 48.5,\n348\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n349\t      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": -20.66\n350\t    },\n351\t    \"tables\": [\n352\t      \"Table 4: DeepSeek CWM row — 标注为 N/A 或 'unparseable >80%'\"\n353\t    ],\n354\t    \"figures\": [],\n355\t    \"analysis\": \"CWM repo 在 DeepSeek 上也失败（worst tier 假设核心之一）。如果两个模型族的 CWM repo\\n都失败，则不能说 \\\"CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific\\\"——需要修改为 \\\"CWM repo failure\\nappears formulation-inherent at 4-8B LoRA scale\\\"。这削弱了原 framing 中\\n\\\"tokenizer-specific\\\" 这个最有 novelty 的 finding。\\n\\n\\nseq2048 比 seq4096/8192 截断更严重，留给 output generation 的 token budget 更少。\\nD124 在 seq8192 下 running_acc=66.9%（31% 完成时 killed），seq4096 下 partial eval\\n显示更差的趋势。seq2048 进一步限制 context → 更多 truncation → 更多 unparseable。\\nQwen CWM repo 在 seq2048 下 65.17% accuracy（已是 failure），DeepSeek 预期更差因为：\\n(1) DeepSeek-Coder tokenizer 的 token 效率对 Python execution output 更低；\\n(2) Epoch 3 过拟合（训练 loss 从 0.021 降到极低但 eval 退化）；\\n(3) 93% unparseable 在 Qwen 上的 pattern 在 DeepSeek 上可能同样严重或更严重。\\nWorst tier 预测 unparseable ≥80%，可用 accuracy 远低于 baseline。\\n\"\n356\t  },\n357\t  {\n358\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-level s42 Epoch 2 (overtraining baseline)\",\n359\t    \"description\": \"D133: DeepSeek CWM repo s42 epoch 2 在 seq2048 下的评估，用于 overtraining 对比\",\n360\t    \"results\": {\n361\t      \"test_accuracy\": 56.8,\n362\t      \"f1_macro\": 47.2,\n363\t      \"f1_fail\": 21.3,\n364\t      \"f1_pass\": 73.1,\n365\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 76.0,\n366\t      \"parseable_only_accuracy\": 53.2,\n367\t      \"epoch3_accuracy\": 52.3,\n368\t      \"overtraining_gap_pp\": 4.5\n369\t    },\n370\t    \"tables\": [\n371\t      \"Appendix: overtraining analysis\"\n372\t    ],\n373\t    \"figures\": [],\n374\t    \"analysis\": \"即使 epoch 2 比 epoch 3 好 4-5pp，仍然在 majority baseline 以下。\\n结论变为 \\\"CWM repo failure 不仅是 overfitting，也是 capacity limitation\\\"。\\n这对叙事有双重影响：(1) 削弱 \\\"只需更多训练调优\\\" 的反驳；\\n(2) 也削弱 \\\"tokenizer-specific\\\" 的 claim（两个模型都失败）。\\n\\n\\nEpoch 2 应比 epoch 3 略好（less overfitting），但差异可能很小（~4pp）。\\n原因：(1) CWM repo 的根本问题是 generation 任务本身在 repo-level context 下太难，\\n不仅仅是 overfitting；(2) eval_loss=NaN 在所有 epoch（已知 DeepSeek issue），\\n无法通过 eval loss 选择最优 epoch；(3) unparseable 问题在 epoch 2 就已存在，\\nepoch 3 只是略微恶化。\\nWorst tier 下 epoch 2 仍然不可用——unparseable ≥76%，accuracy 远低于 baseline。\\nOvertraining 可能存在但不是主要原因（根本原因是 formulation + scale mismatch）。\\n\"\n375\t  },\n376\t  {\n377\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-level s123 (seed 123 replication)\",\n378\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek CWM repo seed=123 训练+评估\",\n379\t    \"results\": {\n380\t      \"training_outcome\": \"训练中途死亡或仅完成 2 epochs\",\n381\t      \"eval_accuracy\": 55.0,\n382\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 80.0,\n383\t      \"f1_macro\": 42.5\n384\t    },\n385\t    \"tables\": [\n386\t      \"Table 4: or Appendix\"\n387\t    ],\n388\t    \"figures\": [],\n389\t    \"analysis\": \"训练中断 + 评估不可用 = deepseek-cwm-repo 完全不可报告。\\nWorst tier 下 Table 4 的 DeepSeek CWM 列标注为 \\\"training failed\\\" 或 \\\"—\\\"。\\n\\n\\nRegistry 显示 s123 训练已中断（D132 notes 提到 \\\"s123 e3 checkpoint 不存在，\\n训练中途死亡\\\"）。只有 epoch 2 checkpoint 可用。Worst tier 下评估结果与 s42\\n类似或更差：unparseable ≥80%，accuracy 远低于 baseline。训练不稳定进一步\\n证实 DeepSeek CWM repo 的 unreliability。\\n\"\n390\t  },\n391\t  {\n392\t    \"name\": \"DeepSeek TRAJ Repo-level (multi-seed, n=48)\",\n393\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B trajectory-level repo verifier，6 seeds\",\n394\t    \"results\": {\n395\t      \"seed_results\": {\n396\t        \"s42\": {\n397\t          \"acc\": 81.25,\n398\t          \"f1_macro\": 80.58\n399\t        },\n400\t        \"s123\": {\n401\t          \"acc\": 75.0,\n402\t          \"f1_macro\": 74.83\n403\t        },\n404\t        \"s0\": {\n405\t          \"acc\": 75.0,\n406\t          \"f1_macro\": 72.68\n407\t        },\n408\t        \"s789\": {\n409\t          \"acc\": 66.67,\n410\t          \"f1_macro\": 62.5\n411\t        },\n412\t        \"s456\": {\n413\t          \"acc\": 75.0,\n414\t          \"f1_macro\": 75.0\n415\t        },\n416\t        \"s999\": {\n417\t          \"acc\": 79.2,\n418\t          \"f1_macro\": 78.57\n419\t        }\n420\t      },\n421\t      \"mean_accuracy\": 75.35,\n422\t      \"std_accuracy\": 4.89,\n423\t      \"majority_baseline\": 54.2,\n424\t      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": 21.15,\n425\t      \"test_set_size\": 48\n426\t    },\n427\t    \"tables\": [\n428\t      \"Table 4: DeepSeek TRAJ row\"\n429\t    ],\n430\t    \"figures\": [],\n431\t    \"analysis\": \"n=48 是 worst tier 的关键弱点。Reviewer 会指出：6 seeds 的 mean 75.35% 的 95% CI\\n约 [70.4, 80.3]（基于 t-distribution），如此宽的 CI 无法做任何有意义的 formulation\\n对比。只能作为 \\\"supplementary evidence that TRAJ is feasible at repo-level\\\" 而非\\ncore finding。\\n\\n\\nTRAJ repo 是唯一跑通的 DeepSeek repo-level formulation。Mean 75.35% 显著超过\\nmajority baseline (54.2%)，但 (1) n=48 太小，CI 极宽；(2) std=4.89% 跨 seed\\n方差巨大（66.67%-81.25%）；(3) 无法与 Qwen TRAJ repo 直接对比因为 Qwen TRAJ repo\\n不存在（只有 CLS 和 CWM）。TRAJ 的 \\\"成功\\\" 可能因为 task 更简单——只需判断\\nresolved/unresolved 而非预测每个 test 的 pass/fail，对 input 质量要求更低。\\n\"\n432\t  },\n433\t  {\n434\t    \"name\": \"Zero-shot Baselines (Qwen + DeepSeek, func + repo)\",\n435\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B 和 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 的零样本基线\",\n436\t    \"results\": {\n437\t      \"qwen_0shot_func_acc\": 68.73,\n438\t      \"deepseek_0shot_func_acc\": 63.02,\n439\t      \"qwen_0shot_repo_acc\": 49.9,\n440\t      \"deepseek_0shot_repo_acc\": 48.54,\n441\t      \"repo_majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n442\t      \"func_majority_baseline\": 51.75\n443\t    },\n444\t    \"tables\": [\n445\t      \"Table 2 & 4: 0-shot baseline row\"\n446\t    ],\n447\t    \"figures\": [],\n448\t    \"analysis\": \"0-shot baseline 建立了 fine-tuning 必要性的论证。Repo-level 0-shot 的灾难表现\\n也解释了为什么 repo-level fine-tuning 如此困难——task 本身在 0-shot 下不可解。\\n\\n\\n0-shot 在 func-level 超过 majority baseline (68.7/63.0 vs 51.75%)，但在 repo-level\\n几乎是 random（49.9/48.5% vs majority 73%）。Repo-level 0-shot 甚至低于 majority\\nbaseline 24pp，说明无 finetuning 的模型完全无法处理 repo-level context。\\nDeepSeek 0-shot 比 Qwen 差 ~5pp，一致 pattern。\\n\"\n449\t  },\n450\t  {\n451\t    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Re-repair (downstream proof-of-concept)\",\n452\t    \"description\": \"用 per-test failure 预测辅助 repair agent 的下游验证\",\n453\t    \"results\": {\n454\t      \"prediction\": \"负面结果或未完成\",\n455\t      \"control_pass1\": 41.0,\n456\t      \"cls_diagnostic_pass1\": 42.5,\n457\t      \"oracle_diagnostic_pass1\": 44.0,\n458\t      \"random_diagnostic_pass1\": 38.0,\n459\t      \"improvement_over_control_pp\": 1.5,\n460\t      \"p_value\": 0.42,\n461\t      \"n_instances\": 44\n462\t    },\n463\t    \"tables\": [],\n464\t    \"figures\": [],\n465\t    \"analysis\": \"Re-repair 负面结果是 worst tier 最大的 downstream utility gap。\\nPaper 必须将 efficiency（6-9x speedup）和 diagnostic granularity 定位为\\nindependent contribution，而非依赖 re-repair 作为 downstream validation。\\nReviewer 会问 \\\"so what's the point of per-test if it doesn't help repair?\\\"——\\n回答需要是 \\\"per-test enables fine-grained verification feedback for developers,\\nnot just automated repair\\\" + \\\"efficiency advantage is standalone\\\"。\\n\\n\\n已有两个 preliminary 实验的负面结果：\\n- re-repair-phase0 (n=10): control 0.82, cls_diag 0.818, oracle_diag 0.809\\n- re-repair-docker-eval (n=44): A1=52.3, A2=43.2, B=36.4, C=38.6, D=40.9\\n两者都未显示 diagnostic information 的有意义改善。核心原因：(1) LLM repair agent\\n已经从 test source code 和 error message 中获取了大部分 diagnostic 信息，\\nper-test classifier 预测（87.5% acc）的额外信号被模型已有信息淹没；\\n(2) 12.5% 的错误预测会误导 repair agent；(3) 样本量太小（n=44）无法检测\\n微小效应。Worst tier 下该实验要么不运行（deadline 压力），要么确认负面结果。\\n\"\n466\t  },\n467\t  {\n468\t    \"name\": \"SWE-bench PerTest Dataset Construction\",\n469\t    \"description\": \"Docker re-evaluation 构建 SWE-bench per-test 数据集\",\n470\t    \"results\": {\n471\t      \"prediction\": \"未完成或仅部分完成\",\n472\t      \"instances_attempted\": 500,\n473\t      \"instances_completed\": 280,\n474\t      \"instances_with_clean_labels\": 220,\n475\t      \"completion_rate\": 0.44,\n476\t      \"label_quality_issues\": \"Docker 环境差异导致约 20% 的 test 结果与原始不一致\"\n477\t    },\n478\t    \"tables\": [],\n479\t    \"figures\": [],\n480\t    \"analysis\": \"SWE-bench PerTest 作为 resource contribution 在 worst tier 下不可用。\\nPaper 只能使用现有 func-level 数据集（CRUXEval-based）+ Qwen repo-level 数据。\\n这进一步限制了 paper 的 contribution breadth。\\n\\n\\n9 天到 deadline，Docker re-evaluation 需要 16-24h 计算 + 环境调试时间。\\nSWE-bench Docker 复现已知困难：(1) Python 版本依赖；(2) package version conflicts；\\n(3) test framework compatibility（pytest vs unittest）；(4) 部分 repo 需要\\nsystem-level dependencies (C extensions, database servers)。\\nWorst tier 下优先级低于 GPU 实验（deepseek repo-level），可能被搁置。\\n即使部分完成，数据质量可能不足以支撑 paper 中的 resource contribution claim。\\n\"\n481\t  },\n482\t  {\n483\t    \"name\": \"Qwen CWM Repo Epoch 2 Eval (D124)\",\n484\t    \"description\": \"Qwen CWM repo-level s42 epoch 2 评估，验证 overtraining\",\n485\t    \"results\": {\n486\t      \"prediction\": \"略好于最终 epoch 但仍不可用\",\n487\t      \"accuracy\": 55.0,\n488\t      \"unparseable_rate\": 88.0,\n489\t      \"parseable_accuracy\": 48.0,\n490\t      \"epoch3_comparison\": \"与 epoch 3 差异 <5pp\"\n491\t    },\n492\t    \"tables\": [\n493\t      \"Appendix: overtraining analysis\"\n494\t    ],\n495\t    \"figures\": [],\n496\t    \"analysis\": \"Overtraining analysis 可以放 appendix 作为 methodological rigor 的证据，\\n但不改变 \\\"CWM repo 在 Qwen 上失败\\\" 的核心结论。\\n\\n\\nQwen CWM repo v10-v12 在最终 epoch 的 unparseable rate 53-93%。Epoch 2 理论上\\n过拟合更少，但 CWM 的核心问题是 generation task 本身对 repo-level 太难，\\n不是 epoch 数量的问题。Qwen tokenizer 在 repo-level output 上的低效率\\n导致即使 epoch 2 也有极高 unparseable rate。如果使用与 v10 相同的\\nmax_new_tokens=64，unparseable 不会显著下降。\\n\"\n497\t  },\n498\t  {\n499\t    \"name\": \"Worst-Tier Repo-level Summary Table 预测\",\n500\t    \"description\": \"Table 4 在 worst tier 下的完整面貌\",\n501\t    \"results\": {\n502\t      \"qwen_cls_4b_test\": 83.63,\n503\t      \"qwen_cls_8b_best_test\": 85.6,\n504\t      \"qwen_cwm_4b_test\": \"N/A (93% unparseable)\",\n505\t      \"qwen_cwm_8b_test\": \"N/A (75% unparseable)\",\n506\t      \"qwen_traj_4b_test\": \"N/A (not trained)\",\n507\t      \"deepseek_cls_test\": \"71.5 (≈majority baseline 73%)\",\n508\t      \"deepseek_cwm_test\": \"N/A (82% unparseable)\",\n509\t      \"deepseek_traj_test\": \"75.35±4.89 (n=48)\",\n510\t      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n511\t      \"cross_model_validated\": false,\n512\t      \"single_model_only\": \"Qwen CLS\"\n513\t    },\n514\t    \"tables\": [\n515\t      \"Table 4\"\n516\t    ],\n517\t    \"figures\": [],\n518\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 的 Table 4 本质上是一个 Qwen CLS 表，其他 cell 都是 N/A 或 ≈baseline。\\n这导致 paper 无法 claim \\\"CLS > CWM at repo-level\\\"（CWM 数据不可用，不是 CLS 更好），\\n也无法 claim cross-model consistency（只有 Qwen）。\\nPaper 必须重新定位 repo-level：不是 \\\"formulation comparison\\\" 而是\\n\\\"case study showing that classification transfers to repo-level while generation collapses\\\"。\\n\\n\\nTable 4 只有两个有意义的 cell：Qwen CLS 4B (83.63%) 和 Qwen CLS 8B (85.60%)。\\n所有 CWM repo 都失败（双模型族）。DeepSeek CLS repo 在 majority baseline 附近。\\nDeepSeek TRAJ repo 有数据但 n=48 + high variance。\\n这意味着 repo-level 的 formulation comparison 完全不成立——\\n只有一种 formulation (CLS) 在一个模型族 (Qwen) 上有效。\\n\"\n519\t  },\n520\t  {\n521\t    \"name\": \"Worst-Tier Paper Contribution 重评估\",\n522\t    \"description\": \"Worst tier 下 paper 三条贡献线的强度评估\",\n523\t    \"results\": {\n524\t      \"contribution_1_formulation_equivalence\": {\n525\t        \"strength\": \"medium\",\n526\t        \"evidence\": \"func-level 双模型族 5-seed TOST p=0.007\",\n527\t        \"weakness\": \"func-level 等价是 predictable; repo-level 无法比较\",\n528\t        \"reviewer_likely_score\": 3.0\n529\t      },\n530\t      \"contribution_2_diagnostic_granularity\": {\n531\t        \"strength\": \"medium-weak\",\n532\t        \"evidence\": \"CLS vs TRAJ 2pp gap + 6-9x speedup + per-test diagnostics\",\n533\t        \"weakness\": \"no downstream validation; 68.7% instances T=1 无额外信息\",\n534\t        \"reviewer_likely_score\": 2.5\n535\t      },\n536\t      \"contribution_3_methodology\": {\n537\t        \"strength\": \"medium\",\n538\t        \"evidence\": \"ICC=0.19, DE=3.97 block-correlation; TOST framework\",\n539\t        \"weakness\": \"niche contribution; may not excite NLP reviewers\",\n540\t        \"reviewer_likely_score\": 3.0\n541\t      },\n542\t      \"overall_expected_score\": 2.75,\n543\t      \"venue_outcome\": \"Borderline Findings (2.5-3.0)\"\n544\t    },\n545\t    \"tables\": [],\n546\t    \"figures\": [],\n547\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 的 paper 策略：\\n1. 放弃 repo-level 作为 core contribution → 降为 \\\"exploratory case study\\\"\\n2. 主推 func-level controlled comparison methodology + statistical rigor\\n3. Block-correlation 作为 \\\"unexpected methodological finding\\\"\\n4. Re-repair 负面结果诚实报告为 future work motivation\\n5. 标题改为聚焦 func-level：\\\"Per-Test vs Trajectory-Level Verification:\\n   A Controlled Study across Formulations and Model Families\\\"\\n6. 投稿目标现实调整：EMNLP Findings 作为 primary goal\\n\\nWorst tier 下三条线都有 solid 数据但没有 breakthrough：\\n(1) Func-level 等价是 well-executed null result 但 predictable；\\n(2) Diagnostic granularity 缺 downstream proof，efficiency 是 engineering 而非 science；\\n(3) Block-correlation 是 novel 但 niche（statistics contribution in NLP venue）。\\n没有一条线单独能达到 EMNLP main 4.0。组合起来 2.5-3.0 = Findings 水平。\\n如果写作极好（clear story + honest scoping），可能 push 到 3.0-3.5。\\n\"\n548\t  }\n549\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36c9cf1b-ce10-4bcf-a0f9-441195ff84d5","uuid":"eba40ebd-134e-4fc9-bebf-3a871f3d53ef","timestamp":"2026-05-18T17:42:10.982Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T171503/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CWM Generation Baseline (Qwen3-4B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B LoRA CWM 生成 baseline，预测 execution output 而非 pass/fail\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_accuracy\": 87.51,\n      \"pass_f1\": 87.31,\n      \"fail_f1\": 87.71,\n      \"exact_match_rate\": 84.02,\n      \"unparseable_predictions\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Func-level formulation comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"func-level CWM=CLS 是 worst tier 的基础支撑——证明 formulation 选择在低复杂度下不重要，\\n这是一个有 statistical backing 的 null result（TOST p=0.007）。\\n\\n\\nFunc-level execution output 短且结构化（通常 <50 tokens），Qwen3-4B 能完美解析。\\nCWM 与 CLS 在 func-level 本质上等价：CWM 先生成 output 再隐式比较，CLS 直接二分类，\\n当 output 空间小时两者信息量一致。87.51% 与 CLS seed42 的 87.83% 在噪声范围内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed Core Comparison (CLS vs CWM vs TRAJ, Qwen3-4B)\",\n    \"description\": \"CLS/CWM 各 5 seeds + TRAJ 4 seeds 的 func-level 多种子验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cls_4b_mean_acc\": 88.43,\n      \"cls_4b_std\": 0.73,\n      \"cls_4b_seeds\": {\n        \"s42\": 87.83,\n        \"s123\": 89.52,\n        \"s456\": 87.88,\n        \"s789\": 89.0,\n        \"s0\": 87.94\n      },\n      \"cwm_4b_mean_acc\": 87.19,\n      \"cwm_4b_std\": 0.37,\n      \"cwm_4b_seeds\": {\n        \"s42\": 87.51,\n        \"s123\": 87.2,\n        \"s456\": 86.98,\n        \"s789\": 86.67,\n        \"s0\": 87.57\n      },\n      \"traj_4b_mean_acc\": 86.46,\n      \"traj_4b_std\": 1.01,\n      \"traj_4b_seeds\": {\n        \"s0\": 85.66,\n        \"s123\": 85.47,\n        \"s456\": 87.4,\n        \"s789\": 87.31\n      },\n      \"pooled_cls_cwm_gap_pp\": -0.45,\n      \"tost_p_value\": 0.0071,\n      \"tost_margin_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"cls_vs_traj_gap_pp\": 1.97\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Func-level formulation comparison\",\n      \"Table 3: Multi-seed statistics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 paper 最 solid 的 statistical result。TOST p=0.007 是 reviewer 难以反驳的。\\n但 novelty concern 在于：func-level 等价本身是 predictable 的（output 短 → 生成不难）。\\n\\n\\n5-seed CLS 和 CWM 的 pooled gap 仅 0.45pp（CWM 略高），TOST 等价检验 p=0.007 在\\n±2pp margin 内确认统计等价。TRAJ 略低 ~2pp 但方差更大（std=1.01 vs 0.73/0.37），\\n反映 trajectory-level aggregation 引入的 problem-level 随机性。三种 formulation\\n在 func-level 的差异不具有实际意义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation (Qwen3-4B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Chain-of-thought 式先推理后判断，测试显式 execution reasoning 是否有帮助\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"conclusion\": \"failed\",\n      \"training_outcome\": \"模型未能学会生成有意义的 execution trace，输出退化为模板化文本\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"负面结果但有叙事价值：证明 \\\"更多推理步骤\\\" 在小模型 + LoRA 场景下不一定有帮助，\\n支持直接分类的 simplicity argument。在 worst tier 下降为 footnote。\\n\\n\\n4B LoRA 容量不足以同时学习 execution reasoning 和 pass/fail 判断。Trace 生成\\n引入了额外的 teacher-forcing 误差累积，且训练数据中没有 ground-truth trace 作为监督。\\n模型要么忽略 trace 直接跳到 label（使 trace 无意义），要么在 trace 阶段积累错误\\n导致最终判断变差。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Trajectory-level Finetuned Baseline (Qwen3-4B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B LoRA trajectory-level verifier (resolved/unresolved)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy\": 85.66,\n      \"unresolved_f1\": 87.5,\n      \"resolved_f1\": 83.18,\n      \"per_test_consistency\": 79.94\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CLS vs TRAJ 的 ~2pp 差距支持 \\\"per-test 粒度不损失精度\\\" 的 claim。但 worst tier\\n下这个差距在 multi-seed 中有时反转（seed456 TRAJ=87.4% > CLS=87.88% 差距仅 0.48pp），\\n需要依赖 TOST 而非 point estimate 来论证。\\n\\n\\nTrajectory-level 将多个 test 聚合为单一 resolved/unresolved 标签，丢失了 per-test\\n粒度信息。85.66% accuracy 低于 per-test CLS 的 88.43% mean，差异来自 aggregation\\n信息损失——当一个 problem 有 n 个 test 时，trajectory 模型需要从更长的拼接 input\\n中做出单一判断，而 CLS 可以独立判断每个 test。per_test_consistency=79.94% 表明\\n约 20% 的 per-test 判断与 trajectory 结论不一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Model Size Scaling (Qwen3-8B CLS vs CWM)\",\n    \"description\": \"8B 模型规模下的 CLS vs CWM 对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cls_8b_mean_acc\": 89.39,\n      \"cls_8b_seeds\": {\n        \"s42\": 90.48,\n        \"s123\": 89.37,\n        \"s456\": 88.31\n      },\n      \"cwm_8b_mean_acc\": 86.96,\n      \"cwm_8b_seeds\": {\n        \"s42\": 87.67,\n        \"s123\": 86.98,\n        \"s456\": 86.24\n      },\n      \"cls_8b_vs_cwm_8b_gap_pp\": 2.43,\n      \"cls_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp\": 0.96,\n      \"cwm_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp\": -0.23\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"8B CLS > CWM 的 gap 比 4B 更明显，但仍然在 func-level。这个结果在所有 tier 共享，\\nworst tier 下支持 \\\"scaling 不帮助 CWM\\\" 的 finding。\\n\\n\\nCLS 从 4B→8B 提升约 1pp（88.43→89.39%），CWM 几乎不变（87.19→86.96%，甚至略降）。\\n这表明 CWM 的瓶颈不在模型容量而在 formulation 本身——生成 exact output 的 ceiling\\n由 exact_match 约束决定，更大模型不能突破。CLS 因为是 binary classification 任务，\\n更大模型的 representation capacity 能略微提升边界样本的判断。8B 规模下 CLS 首次\\n明确超过 CWM（2.43pp gap，超出 multi-seed 噪声范围）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LLM Judge Zero-shot Baseline (Qwen3-8B/32B)\",\n    \"description\": \"零样本 LLM-as-judge 基线，per-test + trajectory-level\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"per_test_8b_acc\": 64.4,\n      \"per_test_32b_acc\": 71.69,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 51.75,\n      \"traj_8b_acc\": 99.1,\n      \"traj_32b_acc\": 99.12,\n      \"traj_8b_true_resolved\": 1,\n      \"traj_8b_pred_resolved\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: as baseline row\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Fine-tuned vs zero-shot 的巨大 gap（87% vs 64-72%）证明 task-specific training\\n的必要性。Zero-shot TRAJ 的 99.1%（=majority baseline）是 cautionary result。\\n\\n\\nPer-test 零样本表现远低于 fine-tuned（64-72% vs 87-90%），因为模型需要理解\\nmutation 引入的 subtle 错误并预测 test 行为，而非简单的 pattern matching。\\nTrajectory-level 99.1% 是虚假高分——模型几乎总是预测 \\\"unresolved\\\"，在 114 个\\nproblem 中只有 1 个是 resolved，majority baseline 就是 99.1%。这暴露了零样本\\ntrajectory-level 评估在极度 imbalanced 场景下的无效性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-test Majority Voting (K=3)\",\n    \"description\": \"Self-consistency 多数投票，测试 K=3 采样是否提升准确率\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy_greedy\": 87.51,\n      \"accuracy_majority_vote\": 86.83,\n      \"delta_pp\": -0.69,\n      \"net_flips\": -13,\n      \"wall_time_ratio\": 4.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"负面结果。排除了一个简单的 improvement avenue，但不影响核心叙事。\\n在 worst tier 下可以放入 appendix 或完全省略。\\n\\n\\nGreedy decoding 在 classification 任务上已接近模型能力上限。K=3 采样引入的随机性\\n对 high-confidence 正确预测无帮助，反而对 low-confidence 边界样本引入噪声：\\n28 个正确→错误 vs 15 个错误→正确 = net -13 flips。CLS 的 decision boundary 是\\ndeterministic 的（logit > 0 → pass），temperature sampling 只会模糊这个边界。\\n这与 generation 任务（如 code generation）中 majority voting 有效不同。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek Func-level Cross-model Validation (CLS + CWM + TRAJ)\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 上重复 func-level 三种 formulation 对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"deepseek_cls_mean\": 86.85,\n      \"deepseek_cls_seeds\": {\n        \"s42\": 86.93,\n        \"s123\": 86.77\n      },\n      \"deepseek_cwm_mean\": 86.83,\n      \"deepseek_cwm_seeds\": {\n        \"s42\": 85.77,\n        \"s123\": 87.88\n      },\n      \"deepseek_traj_mean\": 84.16,\n      \"deepseek_traj_seeds\": {\n        \"v2\": 83.24,\n        \"v2_s123\": 85.08\n      },\n      \"deepseek_cwm_unparseable_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_model_cls_cwm_gap_pp\": 0.02,\n      \"cross_model_cls_traj_gap_pp\": 2.69\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: DeepSeek rows\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Func-level 双模型族验证完整且 clean。CLS≈CWM 在两个模型族都成立。\\n这是 worst tier 最强的跨模型证据，但 reviewer 会认为 func-level 等价本身 novelty 低。\\n\\n\\nDeepSeek func-level 重现了 Qwen 的 pattern：CLS≈CWM（86.85 vs 86.83%，gap 0.02pp），\\nTRAJ 略低（84.16%，gap ~2.7pp）。注意 DeepSeek CWM unparseable=0%，与 Qwen CWM\\nfunc-level 一致——func-level output 足够短，两种 tokenizer 都能完美解析。\\nDeepSeek TRAJ 比 Qwen TRAJ 低 ~2pp，可能因为 DeepSeek-Coder 的 instruction-following\\n能力在 trajectory aggregation 场景下略弱。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-test Failure Prediction Precision/Recall\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-test 粒度的 failure 预测精度分析\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy\": 87.51,\n      \"fail_precision\": 82.75,\n      \"fail_recall\": 93.64,\n      \"fail_f1\": 87.86,\n      \"best_mutation\": \"return_value (97.26%)\",\n      \"worst_mutation\": \"off_by_one (82.56%)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: Per-test diagnostic quality\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Diagnostic granularity 分析完整。但没有 downstream 验证（re-repair 为负），\\nworst tier 下只能声称 \\\"potentially useful for debugging\\\" 而非 \\\"proven useful\\\"。\\n\\n\\nHigh recall (93.64%) 意味着模型捕获了绝大多数真实 failure，但 precision (82.75%)\\n说明约 17% 的 failure 预测是误报。这在 diagnostic 场景下是可接受的——宁可多报\\nfailure 也不要漏掉（fail-safe 偏好）。Mutation type 分析显示 return_value mutations\\n最容易检测（明显的输出差异），off_by_one 最难（微妙的边界差异）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"按 failing test 数量分层的 oracle advantage 分析\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"T1_pct\": 68.7,\n      \"T1_block_adv\": -0.09,\n      \"T2_pct\": 19.1,\n      \"T2_block_adv\": 31.69,\n      \"T3_5_block_adv\": 40.74,\n      \"T6plus_block_adv\": 40.06,\n      \"overall_block_adv\": 10.93,\n      \"T2_contribution_pct\": 55.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Oracle analysis 显示 per-test 的理论优势存在但受限于 T=1 dominance。\\nWorst tier 下 reviewer 会指出 \\\"68.7% 的 instances per-test 不提供额外信息\\\"。\\n\\n\\n68.7% 的 instances 只有 1 个 failing test (T=1)，此时 per-test 和 trajectory-level\\n信息等价（只有一个 test 决定成败）。Per-test 优势集中在 T≥2（31.5% 的 instances），\\n其中 T=2 贡献了 55.3% 的总 advantage。这是因为 T=2 时 per-test 能区分 \\\"一个 test fail\\\"\\nvs \\\"两个 test fail\\\" 而 trajectory 只能说 \\\"unresolved\\\"。T≥3 的 advantage 更大但\\ninstance 更少。SWE-bench 的 median F2P=1 限制了 per-test 的 practical impact。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"验证 per-test predictions 的 intra-problem 相关性结构\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"icc\": 0.1909,\n      \"icc_p_value\": 0.0,\n      \"design_effect\": 3.9676,\n      \"all_correct_observed\": 46,\n      \"all_correct_expected_iid\": 16.35,\n      \"all_correct_ratio\": 2.81\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7: Block correlation analysis\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是一个 methodological contribution：揭示 per-test evaluation 中 i.i.d. 假设\\n不成立，标准 CI 会低估 variance。ICC=0.19 + DE=3.97 是 clean statistical result。\\nWorst tier 下这可能是最独特的贡献——之前没有工作量化过 per-test verification 中的\\nintra-problem correlation。但 reviewer 可能认为这更适合 statistics 会议。\\n\\n\\nICC=0.19 表明同一 problem 内的 per-test 预测错误有显著相关性（p<0.001），\\ndesign effect=3.97 意味着 effective sample size 约为 nominal 的 1/4。\\nObserved all-correct rate (46/114=40.4%) 远高于 i.i.d. 预期 (14.3%)，\\nratio=2.81 说明模型错误在 problem 内是 clustered 的——要么全对，要么错多个。\\n这挑战了 per-test evaluation 中常见的 i.i.d. 假设。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Oracle Total (F2P+P2P) Validated\",\n    \"description\": \"包含 P2P regression tests 的 oracle advantage 验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_reg5pct_block_adv\": -0.005,\n      \"total_reg10pct_block_adv\": 0.083,\n      \"total_reg20pct_block_adv\": 0.278,\n      \"total_reg5pct_pass\": false,\n      \"total_reg10pct_pass\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6 extended\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"P2P 在低 regression rate 下无帮助甚至有害。Worst tier 下这个发现缩窄了 per-test\\n的 applicable scope，reviewer 会用这个来质疑 practical significance。\\n\\n\\nP2P regression rate ≤5% 时 per-test advantage 消失（-0.5pp），因为 P2P tests\\n几乎全 pass，不提供 discriminative 信息。只有 regression rate ≥10% 时 per-test\\n才有正 advantage。实际 regression rate 通常 <5%（高质量修复），这意味着\\nper-test 的优势主要在 F2P tests 上，P2P tests 是 noise source。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Repo-level CLS (Qwen3-4B, best checkpoint)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B LoRA repo-level classification，最优 checkpoint 评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"best_checkpoint\": \"ckpt-4600\",\n      \"test_accuracy\": 83.63,\n      \"test_f1_macro\": 75.63,\n      \"test_fail_f1\": 61.67,\n      \"test_pass_f1\": 89.59,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": 10.67,\n      \"val_accuracy\": 90.07,\n      \"val_test_gap_pp\": 6.44\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: Repo-level comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"83.63% 在 worst tier 范围 [83, 86] 的下端。只有 Qwen 一个模型族达到这个水平，\\nreviewer 会质疑 generalizability。\\n\\n\\nRepo-level CLS 在 Qwen3-4B 上达到 83.63% test accuracy，显著超过 majority baseline\\n10.67pp。但 val-test gap 高达 6.44pp 暴露了 overfitting 或 distribution shift。\\nFail_f1 仅 61.67%（vs func-level 88%），说明 repo-level 的长 context + 复杂依赖\\n大幅增加了分类难度。这是 worst tier Qwen repo-level 的 reference point。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Repo-level CLS (Qwen3-8B, best configurations)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B LoRA repo-level classification，多 seed 多 checkpoint\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"best_s42_ckpt\": \"ckpt-400\",\n      \"best_s42_test_acc\": 84.79,\n      \"best_s123_ckpt\": \"ckpt-3000\",\n      \"best_s123_test_acc\": 85.6,\n      \"best_s123_val_acc\": 88.69,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"85.60% 是 Qwen repo-level CLS 的 ceiling。但 checkpoint 选择的高度敏感性\\n削弱了结果的可靠性。Worst tier 下 reviewer 会质问 \\\"你怎么选 checkpoint\\\"。\\n\\n\\n8B 比 4B 提升 1-2pp（84.79/85.60 vs 83.63），但 s42 和 s123 的 best checkpoint\\n差异巨大（ckpt-400 vs ckpt-3000），暗示 repo-level 训练对 seed 和 checkpoint\\n选择极度敏感。Overfitting 严重——s42 继续训练到 ckpt-1000+ 后 accuracy 反而\\n下降到 83-84%。这种 instability 是 reviewer concern 的来源。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Repo-level CWM (Qwen, all versions)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3 repo-level CWM generation，v3-v12 全部尝试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"v10_accuracy\": 69.91,\n      \"v10_unparseable_pct\": 93.0,\n      \"v11_accuracy\": 66.6,\n      \"v11_unparseable_pct\": 75.2,\n      \"v12_accuracy\": 58.04,\n      \"v12_unparseable_pct\": 53.7,\n      \"best_parseable_accuracy\": \"~42-58% (估计)\",\n      \"all_versions_below_majority\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: CWM row\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CWM repo-level 在 Qwen 上彻底失败。Worst tier 下无法报告有意义的 CWM repo accuracy，\\n只能报告 unparseable rate 作为 negative finding。但这反而支持 \\\"CWM failure 是\\ntokenizer-specific\\\" 的 claim——如果 DeepSeek CWM repo 也失败（worst tier 假设），\\n则需要修改为 \\\"CWM repo failure 可能是 formulation-inherent at small model scale\\\"。\\n\\n\\nQwen tokenizer 在 repo-level 长 output 生成中灾难性失败。v10（max_new_tokens=64）\\n93% unparseable——token budget 太小无法生成完整 execution output。放宽到更大 budget\\n后 v12 unparseable 降到 53.7% 但 accuracy 更差（58%）——模型在长生成中 drift。\\nQwen3 的 tokenizer 对结构化 execution output 的 token 效率极低，是 model-specific\\nfailure 而非 formulation-inherent failure。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-level v5 (seed42, full 3 epochs)\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B repo-level CLS，v5 完整 3 epoch 训练\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_outcome\": \"完成但 acc 未超过 majority baseline\",\n      \"test_accuracy\": 71.5,\n      \"f1_macro\": 54.2,\n      \"f1_fail\": 28.3,\n      \"f1_pass\": 80.1,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": -1.46,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 0.01,\n      \"confusion_pattern\": \"严重偏向预测 pass，recall_fail < 20%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: DeepSeek CLS row — 标注为 ≈baseline 或 below baseline\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DeepSeek CLS repo v1-v5 全部失败。s123 的 74.93% 是唯一勉强高于 baseline 的数据点，\\n但 f1_fail=22.84% 说明模型几乎不能识别 failure（几乎全预测 pass）。\\nWorst tier 叙事：DeepSeek repo-level CLS 不可用，repo-level 比较仅限 Qwen。\\n\\n\\nv4（2 epoch 不完整）eval_loss=NaN 所有 epoch，process killed。v5 是 v4 的完整重跑。\\nv4 已有的 ckpt-200 eval（71.37% acc）低于 majority baseline。s123 的完整训练\\n也只达到 74.93%（勉强高于 73% baseline），且 recall_fail=13.72% 几乎不识别 fail。\\nDeepSeek-Coder 在 repo-level 的核心问题：(1) max_seq_length=2048 对 repo context\\n截断过多（平均 repo input ~5000 tokens），丢失关键依赖信息；(2) 6.7B LoRA 容量\\n不足以学习 repo-level 的复杂 pass/fail pattern；(3) eval_loss=NaN 暗示训练不稳定，\\n3 epoch 可能过拟合或 loss landscape 有 pathological region。\\nWorst tier 预测 v5 在 70-73% 范围，不超过 majority baseline。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CLS Repo-level s123 (seed123)\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B repo-level CLS seed=123 的评估结果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"test_accuracy\": 74.93,\n      \"f1_macro\": 53.94,\n      \"f1_fail\": 22.84,\n      \"f1_pass\": 85.03,\n      \"recall_fail\": 13.72,\n      \"recall_pass\": 97.62,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": 1.97\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这个结果已经 confirm worst-tier 假设。DeepSeek CLS repo essentially at majority baseline。\\nCombined with v5 prediction, worst tier 叙事完全成立。\\n\\n\\n74.93% 仅比 majority baseline 高 1.97pp。F1_fail=22.84% 揭示模型几乎完全\\ncollapse 到 majority class (pass)：recall_fail=13.72% 意味着 86% 的真实 failure\\n被误判为 pass。这不是一个有用的分类器——一个简单的 \\\"always predict pass\\\" baseline\\n就能达到 73%。Gap 1.97pp 在 multi-seed 噪声范围内不可靠。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-level s42 Epoch 3 (canonical seq2048)\",\n    \"description\": \"D131: DeepSeek CWM repo s42 epoch 3 在 canonical seq2048 下的评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"test_accuracy\": 52.3,\n      \"f1_macro\": 44.8,\n      \"f1_fail\": 18.5,\n      \"f1_pass\": 71.1,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 82.0,\n      \"unparseable_count\": 8023,\n      \"parseable_only_accuracy\": 48.5,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": -20.66\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: DeepSeek CWM row — 标注为 N/A 或 'unparseable >80%'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CWM repo 在 DeepSeek 上也失败（worst tier 假设核心之一）。如果两个模型族的 CWM repo\\n都失败，则不能说 \\\"CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific\\\"——需要修改为 \\\"CWM repo failure\\nappears formulation-inherent at 4-8B LoRA scale\\\"。这削弱了原 framing 中\\n\\\"tokenizer-specific\\\" 这个最有 novelty 的 finding。\\n\\n\\nseq2048 比 seq4096/8192 截断更严重，留给 output generation 的 token budget 更少。\\nD124 在 seq8192 下 running_acc=66.9%（31% 完成时 killed），seq4096 下 partial eval\\n显示更差的趋势。seq2048 进一步限制 context → 更多 truncation → 更多 unparseable。\\nQwen CWM repo 在 seq2048 下 65.17% accuracy（已是 failure），DeepSeek 预期更差因为：\\n(1) DeepSeek-Coder tokenizer 的 token 效率对 Python execution output 更低；\\n(2) Epoch 3 过拟合（训练 loss 从 0.021 降到极低但 eval 退化）；\\n(3) 93% unparseable 在 Qwen 上的 pattern 在 DeepSeek 上可能同样严重或更严重。\\nWorst tier 预测 unparseable ≥80%，可用 accuracy 远低于 baseline。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-level s42 Epoch 2 (overtraining baseline)\",\n    \"description\": \"D133: DeepSeek CWM repo s42 epoch 2 在 seq2048 下的评估，用于 overtraining 对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"test_accuracy\": 56.8,\n      \"f1_macro\": 47.2,\n      \"f1_fail\": 21.3,\n      \"f1_pass\": 73.1,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 76.0,\n      \"parseable_only_accuracy\": 53.2,\n      \"epoch3_accuracy\": 52.3,\n      \"overtraining_gap_pp\": 4.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Appendix: overtraining analysis\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"即使 epoch 2 比 epoch 3 好 4-5pp，仍然在 majority baseline 以下。\\n结论变为 \\\"CWM repo failure 不仅是 overfitting，也是 capacity limitation\\\"。\\n这对叙事有双重影响：(1) 削弱 \\\"只需更多训练调优\\\" 的反驳；\\n(2) 也削弱 \\\"tokenizer-specific\\\" 的 claim（两个模型都失败）。\\n\\n\\nEpoch 2 应比 epoch 3 略好（less overfitting），但差异可能很小（~4pp）。\\n原因：(1) CWM repo 的根本问题是 generation 任务本身在 repo-level context 下太难，\\n不仅仅是 overfitting；(2) eval_loss=NaN 在所有 epoch（已知 DeepSeek issue），\\n无法通过 eval loss 选择最优 epoch；(3) unparseable 问题在 epoch 2 就已存在，\\nepoch 3 只是略微恶化。\\nWorst tier 下 epoch 2 仍然不可用——unparseable ≥76%，accuracy 远低于 baseline。\\nOvertraining 可能存在但不是主要原因（根本原因是 formulation + scale mismatch）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek CWM Repo-level s123 (seed 123 replication)\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek CWM repo seed=123 训练+评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_outcome\": \"训练中途死亡或仅完成 2 epochs\",\n      \"eval_accuracy\": 55.0,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 80.0,\n      \"f1_macro\": 42.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: or Appendix\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"训练中断 + 评估不可用 = deepseek-cwm-repo 完全不可报告。\\nWorst tier 下 Table 4 的 DeepSeek CWM 列标注为 \\\"training failed\\\" 或 \\\"—\\\"。\\n\\n\\nRegistry 显示 s123 训练已中断（D132 notes 提到 \\\"s123 e3 checkpoint 不存在，\\n训练中途死亡\\\"）。只有 epoch 2 checkpoint 可用。Worst tier 下评估结果与 s42\\n类似或更差：unparseable ≥80%，accuracy 远低于 baseline。训练不稳定进一步\\n证实 DeepSeek CWM repo 的 unreliability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeepSeek TRAJ Repo-level (multi-seed, n=48)\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B trajectory-level repo verifier，6 seeds\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed_results\": {\n        \"s42\": {\n          \"acc\": 81.25,\n          \"f1_macro\": 80.58\n        },\n        \"s123\": {\n          \"acc\": 75.0,\n          \"f1_macro\": 74.83\n        },\n        \"s0\": {\n          \"acc\": 75.0,\n          \"f1_macro\": 72.68\n        },\n        \"s789\": {\n          \"acc\": 66.67,\n          \"f1_macro\": 62.5\n        },\n        \"s456\": {\n          \"acc\": 75.0,\n          \"f1_macro\": 75.0\n        },\n        \"s999\": {\n          \"acc\": 79.2,\n          \"f1_macro\": 78.57\n        }\n      },\n      \"mean_accuracy\": 75.35,\n      \"std_accuracy\": 4.89,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 54.2,\n      \"gap_vs_baseline_pp\": 21.15,\n      \"test_set_size\": 48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: DeepSeek TRAJ row\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"n=48 是 worst tier 的关键弱点。Reviewer 会指出：6 seeds 的 mean 75.35% 的 95% CI\\n约 [70.4, 80.3]（基于 t-distribution），如此宽的 CI 无法做任何有意义的 formulation\\n对比。只能作为 \\\"supplementary evidence that TRAJ is feasible at repo-level\\\" 而非\\ncore finding。\\n\\n\\nTRAJ repo 是唯一跑通的 DeepSeek repo-level formulation。Mean 75.35% 显著超过\\nmajority baseline (54.2%)，但 (1) n=48 太小，CI 极宽；(2) std=4.89% 跨 seed\\n方差巨大（66.67%-81.25%）；(3) 无法与 Qwen TRAJ repo 直接对比因为 Qwen TRAJ repo\\n不存在（只有 CLS 和 CWM）。TRAJ 的 \\\"成功\\\" 可能因为 task 更简单——只需判断\\nresolved/unresolved 而非预测每个 test 的 pass/fail，对 input 质量要求更低。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Zero-shot Baselines (Qwen + DeepSeek, func + repo)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-4B 和 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 的零样本基线\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_0shot_func_acc\": 68.73,\n      \"deepseek_0shot_func_acc\": 63.02,\n      \"qwen_0shot_repo_acc\": 49.9,\n      \"deepseek_0shot_repo_acc\": 48.54,\n      \"repo_majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"func_majority_baseline\": 51.75\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 & 4: 0-shot baseline row\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"0-shot baseline 建立了 fine-tuning 必要性的论证。Repo-level 0-shot 的灾难表现\\n也解释了为什么 repo-level fine-tuning 如此困难——task 本身在 0-shot 下不可解。\\n\\n\\n0-shot 在 func-level 超过 majority baseline (68.7/63.0 vs 51.75%)，但在 repo-level\\n几乎是 random（49.9/48.5% vs majority 73%）。Repo-level 0-shot 甚至低于 majority\\nbaseline 24pp，说明无 finetuning 的模型完全无法处理 repo-level context。\\nDeepSeek 0-shot 比 Qwen 差 ~5pp，一致 pattern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Re-repair (downstream proof-of-concept)\",\n    \"description\": \"用 per-test failure 预测辅助 repair agent 的下游验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"prediction\": \"负面结果或未完成\",\n      \"control_pass1\": 41.0,\n      \"cls_diagnostic_pass1\": 42.5,\n      \"oracle_diagnostic_pass1\": 44.0,\n      \"random_diagnostic_pass1\": 38.0,\n      \"improvement_over_control_pp\": 1.5,\n      \"p_value\": 0.42,\n      \"n_instances\": 44\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Re-repair 负面结果是 worst tier 最大的 downstream utility gap。\\nPaper 必须将 efficiency（6-9x speedup）和 diagnostic granularity 定位为\\nindependent contribution，而非依赖 re-repair 作为 downstream validation。\\nReviewer 会问 \\\"so what's the point of per-test if it doesn't help repair?\\\"——\\n回答需要是 \\\"per-test enables fine-grained verification feedback for developers,\\nnot just automated repair\\\" + \\\"efficiency advantage is standalone\\\"。\\n\\n\\n已有两个 preliminary 实验的负面结果：\\n- re-repair-phase0 (n=10): control 0.82, cls_diag 0.818, oracle_diag 0.809\\n- re-repair-docker-eval (n=44): A1=52.3, A2=43.2, B=36.4, C=38.6, D=40.9\\n两者都未显示 diagnostic information 的有意义改善。核心原因：(1) LLM repair agent\\n已经从 test source code 和 error message 中获取了大部分 diagnostic 信息，\\nper-test classifier 预测（87.5% acc）的额外信号被模型已有信息淹没；\\n(2) 12.5% 的错误预测会误导 repair agent；(3) 样本量太小（n=44）无法检测\\n微小效应。Worst tier 下该实验要么不运行（deadline 压力），要么确认负面结果。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SWE-bench PerTest Dataset Construction\",\n    \"description\": \"Docker re-evaluation 构建 SWE-bench per-test 数据集\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"prediction\": \"未完成或仅部分完成\",\n      \"instances_attempted\": 500,\n      \"instances_completed\": 280,\n      \"instances_with_clean_labels\": 220,\n      \"completion_rate\": 0.44,\n      \"label_quality_issues\": \"Docker 环境差异导致约 20% 的 test 结果与原始不一致\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SWE-bench PerTest 作为 resource contribution 在 worst tier 下不可用。\\nPaper 只能使用现有 func-level 数据集（CRUXEval-based）+ Qwen repo-level 数据。\\n这进一步限制了 paper 的 contribution breadth。\\n\\n\\n9 天到 deadline，Docker re-evaluation 需要 16-24h 计算 + 环境调试时间。\\nSWE-bench Docker 复现已知困难：(1) Python 版本依赖；(2) package version conflicts；\\n(3) test framework compatibility（pytest vs unittest）；(4) 部分 repo 需要\\nsystem-level dependencies (C extensions, database servers)。\\nWorst tier 下优先级低于 GPU 实验（deepseek repo-level），可能被搁置。\\n即使部分完成，数据质量可能不足以支撑 paper 中的 resource contribution claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen CWM Repo Epoch 2 Eval (D124)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen CWM repo-level s42 epoch 2 评估，验证 overtraining\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"prediction\": \"略好于最终 epoch 但仍不可用\",\n      \"accuracy\": 55.0,\n      \"unparseable_rate\": 88.0,\n      \"parseable_accuracy\": 48.0,\n      \"epoch3_comparison\": \"与 epoch 3 差异 <5pp\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Appendix: overtraining analysis\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Overtraining analysis 可以放 appendix 作为 methodological rigor 的证据，\\n但不改变 \\\"CWM repo 在 Qwen 上失败\\\" 的核心结论。\\n\\n\\nQwen CWM repo v10-v12 在最终 epoch 的 unparseable rate 53-93%。Epoch 2 理论上\\n过拟合更少，但 CWM 的核心问题是 generation task 本身对 repo-level 太难，\\n不是 epoch 数量的问题。Qwen tokenizer 在 repo-level output 上的低效率\\n导致即使 epoch 2 也有极高 unparseable rate。如果使用与 v10 相同的\\nmax_new_tokens=64，unparseable 不会显著下降。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Worst-Tier Repo-level Summary Table 预测\",\n    \"description\": \"Table 4 在 worst tier 下的完整面貌\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_cls_4b_test\": 83.63,\n      \"qwen_cls_8b_best_test\": 85.6,\n      \"qwen_cwm_4b_test\": \"N/A (93% unparseable)\",\n      \"qwen_cwm_8b_test\": \"N/A (75% unparseable)\",\n      \"qwen_traj_4b_test\": \"N/A (not trained)\",\n      \"deepseek_cls_test\": \"71.5 (≈majority baseline 73%)\",\n      \"deepseek_cwm_test\": \"N/A (82% unparseable)\",\n      \"deepseek_traj_test\": \"75.35±4.89 (n=48)\",\n      \"majority_baseline\": 72.96,\n      \"cross_model_validated\": false,\n      \"single_model_only\": \"Qwen CLS\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 的 Table 4 本质上是一个 Qwen CLS 表，其他 cell 都是 N/A 或 ≈baseline。\\n这导致 paper 无法 claim \\\"CLS > CWM at repo-level\\\"（CWM 数据不可用，不是 CLS 更好），\\n也无法 claim cross-model consistency（只有 Qwen）。\\nPaper 必须重新定位 repo-level：不是 \\\"formulation comparison\\\" 而是\\n\\\"case study showing that classification transfers to repo-level while generation collapses\\\"。\\n\\n\\nTable 4 只有两个有意义的 cell：Qwen CLS 4B (83.63%) 和 Qwen CLS 8B (85.60%)。\\n所有 CWM repo 都失败（双模型族）。DeepSeek CLS repo 在 majority baseline 附近。\\nDeepSeek TRAJ repo 有数据但 n=48 + high variance。\\n这意味着 repo-level 的 formulation comparison 完全不成立——\\n只有一种 formulation (CLS) 在一个模型族 (Qwen) 上有效。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Worst-Tier Paper Contribution 重评估\",\n    \"description\": \"Worst tier 下 paper 三条贡献线的强度评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"contribution_1_formulation_equivalence\": {\n        \"strength\": \"medium\",\n        \"evidence\": \"func-level 双模型族 5-seed TOST p=0.007\",\n        \"weakness\": \"func-level 等价是 predictable; repo-level 无法比较\",\n        \"reviewer_likely_score\": 3.0\n      },\n      \"contribution_2_diagnostic_granularity\": {\n        \"strength\": \"medium-weak\",\n        \"evidence\": \"CLS vs TRAJ 2pp gap + 6-9x speedup + per-test diagnostics\",\n        \"weakness\": \"no downstream validation; 68.7% instances T=1 无额外信息\",\n        \"reviewer_likely_score\": 2.5\n      },\n      \"contribution_3_methodology\": {\n        \"strength\": \"medium\",\n        \"evidence\": \"ICC=0.19, DE=3.97 block-correlation; TOST framework\",\n        \"weakness\": \"niche contribution; may not excite NLP reviewers\",\n        \"reviewer_likely_score\": 3.0\n      },\n      \"overall_expected_score\": 2.75,\n      \"venue_outcome\": \"Borderline Findings (2.5-3.0)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 的 paper 策略：\\n1. 放弃 repo-level 作为 core contribution → 降为 \\\"exploratory case study\\\"\\n2. 主推 func-level controlled comparison methodology + statistical rigor\\n3. Block-correlation 作为 \\\"unexpected methodological finding\\\"\\n4. Re-repair 负面结果诚实报告为 future work motivation\\n5. 标题改为聚焦 func-level：\\\"Per-Test vs Trajectory-Level Verification:\\n   A Controlled Study across Formulations and Model Families\\\"\\n6. 投稿目标现实调整：EMNLP Findings 作为 primary goal\\n\\nWorst tier 下三条线都有 solid 数据但没有 breakthrough：\\n(1) Func-level 等价是 well-executed null result 但 predictable；\\n(2) Diagnostic granularity 缺 downstream proof，efficiency 是 engineering 而非 science；\\n(3) Block-correlation 是 novel 但 niche（statistics contribution in NLP venue）。\\n没有一条线单独能达到 EMNLP main 4.0。组合起来 2.5-3.0 = Findings 水平。\\n如果写作极好（clear story + honest scoping），可能 push 到 3.0-3.5。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":549,"startLine":1,"totalLines":549}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01U5e21HPky76XBZCt6TQWwd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me synthesize the key information:\n\n**Tier: worst** - This is the pessimistic scenario. Key characteristics:\n- Repo-level results are weak (only Qwen CLS works, DeepSeek fails)\n- CWM repo-level fails on both model families (not just tokenizer-specific)\n- Re-repair downstream validation is negative\n- Target: EMNLP Findings (score 2.5-3.0)\n\n**Core story for worst tier:**\n\n\nAt the function level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ perform equivalently across both model families with statistical significance (TOST p=0.007), which is a clean null result but not particularly novel. The repo-level findings are more interesting—only Qwen's CLS approach shows improvement while CWM completely fails on both models and DeepSeek's CLS barely outperforms the majority baseline. The methodological contributions center on block-correlation analysis with modest ICC values and TOST equivalence testing, plus per-test diagnostic granularity achieving strong fail recall. The negative results are substantial: re-repair doesn't improve performance, majority voting doesn't help, and the trace-then-judge approach fails to add value.\n\nNow I'm structuring the full paper with sections for abstract, introduction, related work, and methods covering the three formulations and experimental setup. The experiments section will include multiple comparison tables across function-level and repo-level results with multi-seed statistics, model scaling analysis, zero-shot baselines, diagnostic quality metrics, oracle analysis, and correlation studies. I'm preparing to write this in ACL/EMNLP LaTeX format.\n\nMapping out all the experiments to their corresponding tables and sections—the core comparisons will use Qwen and DeepSeek models with multiple seeds, I'll include ablations for trace-then-judge and trajectory-level finetuning, model size scaling with 8B variants, zero-shot LLM judge baselines, per-test majority voting analysis, failure prediction diagnostics, and oracle stratified results—making sure every number comes directly from the experiment data. I'm mapping out the remaining experimental results and their placement in the paper, then setting constraints for the writing itself—avoiding certain punctuation and stylistic patterns while anchoring the narrative around the function-level comparison as the core story with repo-level analysis as a secondary Qwen-focused examination, plus the block correlation as a key methodological contribution.\n\nNow I'm drafting the paper structure using a standard LaTeX article class, settling on a title that captures the main comparison between per-test and trajectory-level verification approaches across different model formulations, and organizing the primary results table to show function-level performance across the model variants.\n\nI'm planning out the supporting tables—one for multi-seed statistical significance testing, another for repository-level aggregation, then diagnostic tables for mutation types, oracle analysis, and correlation patterns. For the paper itself, I'm aiming for a concise structure that covers the key experiments without unnecessary length, starting with an abstract around 200 words.\n\nWriting the LaTeX now to flesh out the full paper with all the results tables and analysis sections. I'm checking that the output directory exists before I start writing the paper.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2054,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15048,"cache_read_input_tokens":25435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15048},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent